cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "oracle-varx: causal lag discovery in confounded time series"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the package and the original paper."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Roudane
    given-names: Merwan
    email: merwanroudane920@gmail.com
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-10-15"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/oracle-varx/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/merwanroudane/oracle-varx"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/oracle-varx/0.1.1/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - econometrics
  - causal discovery
  - Granger causality
  - vector autoregression
  - double machine learning
  - false discovery rate
abstract: >-
  A Python implementation of ORACLE-VARX: double/debiased machine learning
  removes nonlinear confounder effects from the outcomes and the lagged series,
  adaptive causal lag estimation selects the lag order in each rolling window by
  sequential significance testing tuned on validation forecasts, and a
  Benjamini-Hochberg step selects directed, lag-annotated edges at a target false
  discovery rate, with a coefficient, a standard error and a confidence interval
  for every edge.
